            <div xml:id="d800">

                <pb facs="1288" n="1192" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg1192"/>

                <head>No. 797.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Beardsley to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Agency and Consulate-General of the United States in
                                Egypt</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Cairo</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1874-05-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 30, 1874</date>. (Received June 30.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 201.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that, by
                    circular from the ministry of foreign affairs, dated the 27th instant, the
                    entire question of judicial reform has been placed in charge of Cherif Pasha,
                    minister of justice, to whom all communications in the future will be addressed,
                    instead of to the minister of foreign affairs as hitherto.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>R. BEARDSLEY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
